            <ArticleTitle>Accurate Design of Low Backscattering Metasurface Using Iterative Fourier Transform Algorithm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11346</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/s41598-017-11719-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An accurate method is proposed to design low-backscattering metasurfaces efficiently using an iterative Fourier transform algorithm, which avoids the large amount of time-consuming numerical simulations of complicated electromagnetic problems and provides satisfactory performance to reduce the backward scattering. As an example of the application, a broadband low-backscattering metasurface is designed, fabricated, and characterized. Both full-wave simulation and measured results reveal that the proposed method offers a rapid and efficient tool to manipulate the scattering behaviors of the metasurface, and thus realizes significant scattering reductions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
